<div>We provide complete UX and UI design services for web, SaaS, and mobile products. This includes user research, wireframing, prototyping, usability testing, and polished UI design.</div>
<div>We also create scalable design systems that ensure consistency across products and platforms. Our goal is to deliver intuitive, conversion-driven designs that drive growth and engagement.</div>
</div>
</div></div></div><div class="faq-item border border-[#E7E7E7] rounded-[16px] p-[16px] md:p-[20px] lg:p-[24px] mb-[16px] md:mb-[24px]"><h3 class="faq-title flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer text-[18px] lg:text-[24px] leading-[1.2] md:leading-[1.13] lg:leading-[32px] font-semibold"><span class="w-[85%]">How does six2eight approach user-centered design?</span><span class="faq-icon transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out "><svg class="max-sm:w-[12px] max-sm:h-[12px]" width="20" height="11" viewBox="0 0 20 11" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1 1L9.29289 9.29289C9.62623 9.62623 9.79289 9.79289 10 9.79289C10.2071 9.79289 10.3738 9.62623 10.7071 9.29289L19 1" stroke="#606060" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span></h3><div class="faq-content overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out max-h-0 mt-0 opacity-0"><div class="text-[18px] leading-[28px] text-[#070707] pb-2"><div>
<div>We follow a human-centered design process focused on real user needs and behaviors.</div>
